{"id": "EUVD-2026-71402", "enisaUuid": "768ed21e-33ae-342d-82f6-15b6adefe444", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_aml: validate firmware segment lengths\n\naml_download_firmware() reads two lengths from the firmware header and\nuses them to build pointers before checking that the header and segment\ndata are present. A truncated or inconsistent firmware image can make\nthe driver read past firmware->data while constructing TCI commands.\n\nReject images shorter than the header and ensure that the ICCM and DCCM\nranges fit within the loaded firmware before downloading either segment.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:12:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:43:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7733b01ed13685773ccda91035a46f87d4cfef7c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e1534d49a7b8ba728e84b020f6d802aa1cb759d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c70253462902d835e843b470f74aa816d60af80", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2763b8bcb504e30ec955474f51b99ce42fc62f3b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2bf6b9baca9372ea51b6d0f2820dc9bf29a83ef4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q3hj-w9xj-vc4p", "CVE-2026-80759"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ca517b5-ec2b-324b-aeb5-697591e4d788", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "37bac77e4649e8158698a60addc22ec4faf5649a <2763b8bcb504e30ec955474f51b99ce42fc62f3b"}, {"id": "0e9f4ad3-6a05-38fe-bf5a-b764cf31dac0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.11"}, {"id": "2c4ba8fa-4db2-3ae7-ba10-3359e6ccf5d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}, {"id": "325b6389-a896-3452-9524-37feaf0e57ba", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4ce4527d-4186-3080-a5cc-7f3c5b7c8d5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "produ